**Issue**: The `player.play()` call and `createAudioPlayer()` lack error handling. Audio playback can fail due to various reasons (invalid source, permissions, system issues), but errors are silently ignored.

**Impact**: If audio playback fails, users and developers will have no feedback about the failure, making debugging difficult.

**Suggested Fix**:
```tsx
const player = createAudioPlayer(source);

// Listen for playback completion to release resources
const subscription = player.addListener('playbackStatusUpdate', (status) => {
    if (status.error) {
        Log.alert('[Sound] Playback error:', {message: status.error});
        subscription.remove();
        player.remove();
        return;
    }

    if (!status.didJustFinish) {
        return;
    }

    subscription.remove();
    player.remove();
});

player.play().catch((error) => {
    Log.alert('[Sound] Failed to play sound:', {message: error.message});
    subscription.remove();
    player.remove();
});
```

